@* The component router.

   It deliberately declares no @rendermode, so anything it reaches is statically
   server-rendered.

   Taxpayer-data screens are NOT reached through this router. `ReviewEndpoints`
   and `ExtractionEndpoints` return strongly typed components only after a
   minimal endpoint has authenticated the caller, revalidated the membership,
   resolved the trusted firm, and completed the firm-scoped read. Routing those
   screens here instead would move the safe-404 and authorization decisions into
   component discovery, and a refused request could render a partial page before
   the refusal was reached. Those page components therefore carry no @page
   directive at all.

   `AppAssembly` is this assembly, so no other assembly can contribute a route. *@

<Router AppAssembly="@typeof(Routes).Assembly">
    <Found Context="routeData">
        <RouteView RouteData="@routeData" DefaultLayout="@typeof(PortalLayout)" />
    </Found>
</Router>
